{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_table", "label": "Per-origin training sub-block budget table", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Per-origin training sub-block (21 months)", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Committed so a Stage 2 run has something to be checked against rather than something to be tuned to; budget.py pins the values instead of recomputing them inside the test, because with both sides computed the same way a regression would agree with itself and pass."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_constants", "label": "Budget constants \u2014 L, H, 119, spacing, 720", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Constants", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_segment_wise_count", "label": "Segment-wise window count \u03a3 max(0, n_i \u2212 119)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Per-origin training sub-block", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The assertion target, because it is the only form that is correct when a segment holds fewer than 120 bars."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_closed_form", "label": "The closed form is an upper bound, not an identity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "What changed against the derived table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "(bars \u2212 119) \u2212 [119 \u00d7 breaks + excluded] equals the segment-wise count only while every segment clears 120 bars. Origin 2022-02 contains an 80-bar segment: it contributes zero windows but the closed form charges it 80 \u2212 119 = \u221239 and absorbs the negative silently. Seven origins are understated by 39 \u2026 137 windows."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_raw_frame", "label": "Raw-frame training range 13,558 \u2026 15,217", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Per-origin training sub-block", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 10.9% spread, monotone in calendar time; largest training tensor 15,217 \u00d7 96 \u00d7 12 \u00d7 4 B = 70.12 MB."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_feature_frame", "label": "Feature-frame training range 13,545 \u2026 15,217", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Raw vs feature frame table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The tensors are cut from the feature frame, which holds one fewer bar per segment because r is computed per segment. The two frames are both right about different things, and the assertion target for a training run is the feature-frame count."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_subsample_floor", "label": "Subsampling floor is 13,545", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Raw vs feature frame table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not 13,558 and emphatically not 13,520 \u2014 the control for the training-volume variation the fixed rolling window was chosen to eliminate."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_test_block_720", "label": "Test blocks hold 720 forecast origins, not 601", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Test blocks hold 720 forecast origins", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Counting test blocks the training way returns 601 of 720 on a perfectly clean block \u2014 a 16.5% phantom loss that would read as outage damage and enter \u00a79.2's block-coverage covariate as pure noise. The two semantics differ by exactly L + H \u2212 1."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_unusable_bars", "label": "Exactly 3 unusable bars, the same 3 in all three senses", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Both previously-unmeasured quantities, answered", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "2019-06-07T21:00, 2021-02-11T03:00, 2023-03-24T12:00. Total unusable is 3, not 9, which follows mechanically: no volume means no trades, and no trades means the bar's high and low never separate."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_committed_train_budget", "label": "budget.py::COMMITTED_TRAIN_BUDGET pinned values", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Header, Regenerating", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Regenerate the table and update the constant in the same commit, never one alone, or the assertion checks the artifact against a stale pin."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_gap_straddle", "label": "Gap blocks straddling a span boundary charged whole", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "What changed against the derived table", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The derivation attributed a block to the span containing its gap_start; the measurement counts only positions actually inside the span. This moves counts in both directions, which is why some origins measured higher than derived and others lower."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_loss_not_random", "label": "Test-window loss is conditioned on future gaps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "What the spread means", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Binance outages cluster on stress, so dropped targets are disproportionately high-volatility ones and survival depends on information unavailable at the forecast origin. A stated limitation, not a fixable defect."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_training_volume_spread", "label": "Training volume is not constant across origins", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "What the spread means", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "13,558 \u2026 15,217, monotone in calendar time and so correlated with the origin index and with everything compared across origins \u2014 partially reintroducing the variation the fixed rolling window was chosen to eliminate."}, {"id": "docs_origin_window_budget_regenerate", "label": "Regenerating the budget table", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Regenerating", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The table is a pure function of data/raw/BTCUSDT_1h.parquet and the constants, asserted by tests/test_data_plane.py."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_origin_window_budget_table", "target": "docs_origin_window_budget_segment_wise_count", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "Per-origin training sub-block", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_origin_window_budget_segment_wise_count", "target": "docs_origin_window_budget_closed_form", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/ORIGIN_WINDOW_BUDGET.md", "source_location": "What changed against the derived table", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_origin_window_budget_table", "target": "docs_origin_window_budget_raw_frame", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.